# Fetched tarballs, source trees, build trees, and the libraries themselves. Nothing built
# belongs in git: the point of this repo is that the *release assets* are the artifacts, and a
# committed .a is one nobody can tell apart from the one CI made.
build/
dist/
.DS_Store

# The same rule, applied to the Rust half. `prebuilt/` is a cache: ./sync-prebuilt.sh fills it
# from dist/, and failing that crates/freerdp-prebuilt-sys/build.rs downloads what it needs from
# the latest release. Nothing about which bytes are correct is stored here — that travels with
# the archives, as SHA256SUMS and each archive's own MANIFEST.
crates/freerdp-prebuilt-sys/prebuilt/
target/
Cargo.lock

# Per-checkout notes for Claude Code: what this particular machine can and cannot build. All of
# it is true of one developer's setup rather than of the project; anything that holds for
# everyone belongs in a committed CLAUDE.md instead.
CLAUDE.local.md
